    systemsLens: "The structure inserts a delay between publication and consumption, and uses the registry community's detection as a filter during that delay. The stock is builds exposed to versions younger than the detection time. The cooldown shrinks it toward zero for fast detected compromises and does nothing for slow ones. The balancing loop is the exception process: too slow and teams disable the cooldown, too loose and it protects nothing.",
    underStress: "It gets stronger as worm style attacks increase, because those are detected fast and the cooldown covers them. It is weak against patient attackers who let a malicious version age, so it must sit alongside provenance and behaviour monitoring. Strength depends on CI enforcement and on exceptions that are rare and visible.",
    adoption: "Enable the minimum release age in the package manager for one repository with a lock file and disable install scripts, allow listing the few that need them. Enforce the same settings in CI. Write the exception procedure on one page and time it. Roll out through the platform template so new projects inherit it. Track yanked versions that were never installed as the measure of value.",
