    structure: "A build request produces a new environment: a virtual machine or hardened container created from a known, measured image, with no state from previous jobs. The builder receives an identity for this job through attestation (the platform knows which workflow and commit it is running) and uses that identity to obtain short lived credentials for exactly what the job needs: read the source, fetch pinned dependencies, write the artefact, request a signing certificate. No long lived secrets are mounted. Network egress is restricted to the registries and services the build requires. The build runs, provenance is generated by the platform (outside the build's control), the artefact and provenance are uploaded, and the environment is destroyed. Caches, if used, are content addressed and verified by hash so a poisoned cache cannot alter output. Any attempt by a build step to reach the signing key or to persist fails because neither exists in the environment.",
